---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
const { s } = Astro.props;
---
<article class="proof-capture" id={`capture-${s.service}`}>
  <header class="capture-heading">
    <span class="pill">{s.title}</span>
    <p class="capture-blurb">{s.blurb}</p>
    <div class="capture-baseline">
      <span class="eyebrow">SURICATA BASELINE</span>
      <strong>{s.suricata.record_count} EVE records</strong>
      <span class={s.suricata.alerts === 0 ? 'baseline-zero' : ''}>{s.suricata.alerts} alerts</span>
      <span class="capture-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <span class="eyebrow">CERNITY → SIEM</span>
      <strong>{s.delivered_count} delivered</strong>
      {s.suppressed_count > 0 && <span>{s.suppressed_count} suppressed as noise</span>}
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="capture-detectors">
    {s.detectors.map((d) => (
      <section class="detector-card">
        <div class="detector-top">
          <code class="detector-id">{d.detector_id}</code>
          <span class={`sev sev-${d.severity >= 8 ? 'high' : d.severity >= 6 ? 'med' : 'low'}`}>sev {d.severity}</span>
          <span class="badge cat">{d.category}</span>
          {d.mitre.map((m) => <span class="badge mitre">{m}</span>)}
          {d.fired_count > 1 && <span class="badge fired">fired {d.fired_count}×</span>}
          {d.delivered
            ? <span class="badge delivered">DELIVERED → SIEM</span>
            : <span class="badge suppressed">SUPPRESSED (noise)</span>}
        </div>
        <h3 class="detector-why">{d.why}</h3>
        <p class="detector-meaning">{d.meaning}</p>

        <div class="record-comparison">
          <section class="record-pane">
            <div class="record-title"><span class="eyebrow">SURICATA → EVE</span><p>Triggering source record · unmodified · 0 alerts raised</p></div>
            <div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${d.detector_id}: source Suricata record`}>
              {d.source_record
                ? <Code code={JSON.stringify(d.source_record, null, 2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" />
                : <p class="record-none">Aggregated across multiple records — see the full source set in the download.</p>}
            </div>
          </section>
          <section class="record-pane">
            {d.delivered && d.siem ? (
              <>
                <div class="record-title"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT THE SOC ANALYST SEES · ELASTICSEARCH</span><p>Stored SIEM document — <code>_index</code> / <code>_id</code> / <code>_source</code></p></div>
                <div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${d.detector_id}: SIEM Elasticsearch document`}>
                  <Code code={JSON.stringify(d.siem.elasticsearch, null, 2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" />
                </div>
                <div class="cef-row"><span class="eyebrow">SAME FINDING · CEF EVENT (syslog SIEM)</span><pre class="cef-line">{d.siem.cef}</pre></div>
              </>
            ) : (
              <>
                <div class="record-title"><span class="eyebrow">CERNITY LIFECYCLE · NOT DELIVERED</span><p>The gate withheld this from the analyst plane</p></div>
                <div class="suppressed-note">
                  <p><strong>state: {d.lifecycle.state}</strong> · devo_delivery_state: {d.lifecycle.devo_delivery_state}</p>
                  <p>{d.lifecycle.suppression_reason}</p>
                  <p class="suppressed-why">Kept in the store for correlation and hunting — it does not add to the analyst's queue. This is how the finding gate reduces SIEM volume instead of only re-ranking it.</p>
                </div>
              </>
            )}
          </section>
        </div>

        <details class="source-records">
          <summary>Detector output before the lifecycle (raw candidate)</summary>
          <div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${d.detector_id}: raw candidate finding`}>
            <Code code={JSON.stringify(d.finding, null, 2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" />
          </div>
        </details>

        <aside class="detector-next">
          <span class="eyebrow">WHAT TO INVESTIGATE</span>
          <ol>{d.investigation.map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol>
        </aside>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="record-caption">
    The left pane is the exact Suricata EVE that triggered the detector; the right is the finalized finding as it reaches the SIEM — the Elasticsearch <code>_source</code> and the CEF event — produced by the real finding-service lifecycle and findings-forwarder, both taken verbatim from the capture. <code>enrichment_state: TIMEOUT</code> means the finding was delivered now and packet evidence would attach only where a forensics overlay is deployed; it is not a failure or a drop.
  </div>
  <div class="case-limit"><strong>What this does not establish</strong><p>{s.limit}</p></div>
  <div class="case-download">
    <a class="text-link" href={`/evidence/detector-stage/${s.service}.json`} download>Download the full capture (source EVE + candidates + delivered SIEM records) ↓</a>
    <span class="capture-provenance">Produced by replaying <code>{s.fixture}</code> through the detector, finding-service, and forwarder code (<code>tools/proof-capture/capture.py</code>) — synthetic fixture input on an in-process pipeline, not a live SIEM cluster or customer incident.</span>
  </div>
</article>
